From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH 0147] mac80211: ath11k: validate wmi event header length

Carry upstream 9ef9dd30058cc9223c72f711dca1a28a5947d0c5 on the selected 6.18.7
backports without a baseline change. Preserve upstream authorship and
sign-offs; hardware acceptance remains separate from offline validation.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/956-wifi-ath11k-validate-wmi-event-header-length.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/956-wifi-ath11k-validate-wmi-event-header-length.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/956-wifi-ath11k-validate-wmi-event-header-length.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+From 9ef9dd30058cc9223c72f711dca1a28a5947d0c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Jeff Johnson <jeff.johnson@oss.qualcomm.com>
+Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:01:31 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: Avoid buffer overread in ath11k_wmi_tlv_op_rx()
+
+Currently, in ath11k_wmi_tlv_op_rx(), the firmware buffer is read
+without first verifying that the buffer has enough data to hold a
+header. This could result in a buffer overread.
+
+Add an upfront length check before dereferencing skb->data as a
+wmi_cmd_hdr. The check is placed before the trace_ath11k_wmi_event()
+call to preserve the existing trace semantics (tracing the full raw
+WMI event including the header), unlike the analogous ath12k fix which
+could use skb_pull_data() directly.
+
+Compile tested only.
+
+Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
+Reviewed-by: Rameshkumar Sundaram <rameshkumar.sundaram@oss.qualcomm.com>
+Reviewed-by: Baochen Qiang <baochen.qiang@oss.qualcomm.com>
+Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260716-ath11k_wmi_tlv_op_rx-overread-v1-1-0b972b3f1368@oss.qualcomm.com
+Signed-off-by: Jeff Johnson <jeff.johnson@oss.qualcomm.com>
+---
+ drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c | 6 ++++--
+ 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+index 2d2c6d7a4a3b4d..4cbd7293845a24 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+@@ -8901,13 +8901,15 @@ static void ath11k_wmi_tlv_op_rx(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
+ 	struct wmi_cmd_hdr *cmd_hdr;
+ 	enum wmi_tlv_event_id id;
+ 
++	if (skb->len < sizeof(*cmd_hdr))
++		goto out;
++
+ 	cmd_hdr = (struct wmi_cmd_hdr *)skb->data;
+ 	id = FIELD_GET(WMI_CMD_HDR_CMD_ID, (cmd_hdr->cmd_id));
+ 
+ 	trace_ath11k_wmi_event(ab, id, skb->data, skb->len);
+ 
+-	if (skb_pull(skb, sizeof(struct wmi_cmd_hdr)) == NULL)
+-		goto out;
++	skb_pull(skb, sizeof(*cmd_hdr));
+ 
+ 	switch (id) {
+ 		/* Process all the WMI events here */
